.TH MOUNT.RUNWAY 8 "" "Runway" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mount.runway \- mount helper for Runway boot stores
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mount \-t runway
[\fB\-o\fR \fIoptions\fR]
.IR store [\fB,\fIstore\fR...]
.I mountpoint
.br
.B mount \-t runway auto
.I mountpoint
.PP
.B mount.runway
.IR store [\fB,\fIstore\fR...]
.I mountpoint
[\fB\-o\fR \fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mount.runway
is called by
.BR mount (8)
for the file system type
.BR runway .
It starts
.BR rwy\-fuse (1)
with the stores and the mount point.
.PP
The stores are separated by commas.
Several stores are the members of one mirror: a write reaches every member, and each member is locked.
A store is a file, a partition (such as
.I /dev/sda2
or
.BI PARTUUID= uuid\fR),
or
.IR image@offset [\fB+\fIlength\fR].
.PP
The store
.B auto
asks
.BR rwyctl (1)
for the members of the boot store
.RB ( "rwyctl members" ):
a partition of the store type, else a
.B RUNWAY.DAT
on a mounted ESP.
The helper waits for udev first, for at most 10 seconds.
It fails (exit 1) when there is no store or when it cannot choose one.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " options"
Passed to
.BR rwy\-fuse (1),
and so to FUSE.
Example:
.BR allow_other ,
.BR default_permissions .
.TP
.B \-r
Same as
.BR "\-o ro" .
.TP
.B \-w
Same as
.BR "\-o rw" .
.PP
The options
.BR \-s ,
.BR \-f ,
.B \-n
and
.BR \-v ,
and
.B \-t
with its value, are accepted and ignored.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUNWAY_FUSE
The program to run instead of
.BR rwy\-fuse .
If
.B rwy\-fuse
is not in the path, the helper looks for it in
.IR /usr/bin ,
.I /usr/local/bin
and
.IR /bin .
.PP
The keys of an encrypted store come from the environment and the TPM, as for
.BR rwy\-fuse (1).
.TP
.B RWYCTL
The program to run instead of
.BR rwyctl ,
for
.BR auto .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/fstab
.PP
.RS
.nf
/efi/RUNWAY.DAT  /boot  runway  defaults  0  0
auto             /boot  runway  defaults  0  0
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
2 for a usage error, 1 when
.B auto
finds no store.
Otherwise the helper is replaced by
.BR rwy\-fuse ,
and its exit status is the one that
.BR mount (8)
sees.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rwy\-fuse (1),
.BR fsck.runway (8),
.BR rwyctl (1)
